ect3D11 vs_5_0 ps_5_0, D3D11-31.0.15.4617) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-7700 CPU @ 3.60GHz (8 threads) - 15.93 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen marking a method with `@abstract`, the \"class_name\" and \"type\" attributes of the \"return\" dictionary in the method info dictionary returned by Script::get_script_method_list and Object::get_method_list gets erased. class_name will always be empty and type will always be 0.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. create a script and mark with the ```@abstract``` annotation\n2. create a method and also mark with the ```@abstract``` annotation\n3. in another test script, on _ready, get the methods information from that script or from an instance of it and see that it returns the unexpected values\n\nThis also can be seen in the screenshot bellow\n\n<img width=\"1226\" height=\"1053\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a3b8f5a1-c54f-4f30-858c-ba5f0c86bce8\" />\n\nAll the scripts look like this, with the exception that A.gd doesn't have any ```@abstract``` annotation, B.gd only annotates the entire script with ```@abstract``` and only C.gd annotates both the script and the method with ```@abstract```.\n\n<img width=\"417\" height=\"124\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/725fb84e-902f-44ef-bad8-71461a905447\" />\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[AbstractMethodInfoBug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22495753/AbstractMethodInfoBug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"http